(2529624, 346092, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - Good potential.  Looks like some gamma issues in the darker areas of the frame.  A more finely tuned crop and variation in composition and slight shift of focus on the frame, make this better in my opinion. edit:typo<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-21 07:57:48.</i></td>', '3 - Good potential.  Looks like some gamma issues in the darker areas of the frame.  A more finely tuned crop and variation in composition and slight shift of focus on the frame, make this better in my opinion. edit:typo', '2006-06-19 19:24:16.000000', '2006-06-21 08:57:48.000000', 1),
(2529637, 346541, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - Like this shot on its own, especially colors - but for this Challenge, struggling to see a true ''framing'' here.</td>', '2 - Like this shot on its own, especially colors - but for this Challenge, struggling to see a true ''framing'' here.', '2006-06-19 19:27:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529645, 347171, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Good.  Despite seemingly beginnings of some gamma type issues in the blacks (and could just be deliberate processing), the processing works well here, except the fact that Jonathan looks a fraction too contrasted - but could also be focal issues.  Visually, just looks like it needs a whisker nudge rotation up on the left - but I can see it might throw out the alignment at the base of the pillars.</td>', '6 - Good.  Despite seemingly beginnings of some gamma type issues in the blacks (and could just be deliberate processing), the processing works well here, except the fact that Jonathan looks a fraction too contrasted - but could also be focal issues.  Visually, just looks like it needs a whisker nudge rotation up on the left - but I can see it might throw out the alignment at the base of the pillars.', '2006-06-19 19:31:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529650, 347445, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Nice.  Good control of the dof.  Difficult, but perhaps a more finely tuned crop, especially left &amp; right, make this better in my opinion.  A little more foliage/branches on the right would have been good but - there ya go.  Also, ''somehow'' just gaining a little more depth/drama - but no idea how, especially in basic.</td>', '6 - Nice.  Good control of the dof.  Difficult, but perhaps a more finely tuned crop, especially left & right, make this better in my opinion.  A little more foliage/branches on the right would have been good but - there ya go.  Also, ''somehow'' just gaining a little more depth/drama - but no idea how, especially in basic.', '2006-06-19 19:33:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529657, 345904, 39850, '<td valign="top">1 - Without your title, on quick glance, no idea what this is.  The framing you have used is compositionally ''off'' plus a silhouette.  Choice of subject within frame does not seem to have been calculated.</td>', '1 - Without your title, on quick glance, no idea what this is.  The framing you have used is compositionally ''off'' plus a silhouette.  Choice of subject within frame does not seem to have been calculated.', '2006-06-19 19:35:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529677, 347416, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - Different - but concept not holding my attention, plus focus on the cd a little better may have helped give this something extra.  The oof effect is quite nice, however for this Challenge, the frame/foreground subject needs to be more dominant &amp; defined overall, in my opinion.  Ultimately, I see a shot of a key viewed through the hole of a cd, without any strong and unusual elements required to make this ''special''.</td>', '2 - Different - but concept not holding my attention, plus focus on the cd a little better may have helped give this something extra.  The oof effect is quite nice, however for this Challenge, the frame/foreground subject needs to be more dominant & defined overall, in my opinion.  Ultimately, I see a shot of a key viewed through the hole of a cd, without any strong and unusual elements required to make this ''special''.', '2006-06-19 19:39:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529681, 347352, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - Like to see the frame in better focus, and perhaps more of it incorporated for added balance compositionally.  A slight nudge rotation up on the right, perhaps a variation in angle, for added ''effect'' and a little further back, make this better in my opinion.</td>', '3 - Like to see the frame in better focus, and perhaps more of it incorporated for added balance compositionally.  A slight nudge rotation up on the right, perhaps a variation in angle, for added ''effect'' and a little further back, make this better in my opinion.', '2006-06-19 19:41:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529685, 347376, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - Despite your title, still think this needs a fairly good rotate up on the left.  A more finely tuned crop to ''use'' the frame more, also would have helped.</td>', '3 - Despite your title, still think this needs a fairly good rotate up on the left.  A more finely tuned crop to ''use'' the frame more, also would have helped.', '2006-06-19 19:41:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529691, 347477, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - Difficult, but more definition and light in the ''frame'' and perhaps overall the colors tweaked for added depth and drama, make this better in my opinion.  Depending what was there, more ''frame'' incorporated bottom/bottom left as well.</td>', '3 - Difficult, but more definition and light in the ''frame'' and perhaps overall the colors tweaked for added depth and drama, make this better in my opinion.  Depending what was there, more ''frame'' incorporated bottom/bottom left as well.', '2006-06-19 19:43:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529710, 347609, 39850, '<td valign="top">4 - Good potential.  Difficult, as I like the oof/bokeh effect in the triangles, however at least part of that ''frame'' in sharper focus, a more finely tuned crop and composition and attention paid to finer details such as skin/make up, make this better in my opinion.  Overall perhaps further back, incorporating more of the ''triangle(s)'' and a slight shift in focus (especially so the skin(?) top left is not so apparent), also help this, in my opinion. edit:typo<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-21 07:57:30.</i></td>', '4 - Good potential.  Difficult, as I like the oof/bokeh effect in the triangles, however at least part of that ''frame'' in sharper focus, a more finely tuned crop and composition and attention paid to finer details such as skin/make up, make this better in my opinion.  Overall perhaps further back, incorporating more of the ''triangle(s)'' and a slight shift in focus (especially so the skin(?) top left is not so apparent), also help this, in my opinion. edit:typo', '2006-06-19 19:47:18.000000', '2006-06-21 08:57:30.000000', 1),
(2529724, 347437, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Nice.  Difficult, but the dof even closer as well, may have made this even better, but would likely have diminished the illusion of the framing at the bottom.  Not sure, but perhaps a more finely tuned crop at the top, making a more horizontal framing.  More at the bottom (even if oof), possibly as well.  Selective desat may have given this extra as well, who knows - nice scene/candid as is, in my opinion.  +m in your title.</td>', '6 - Nice.  Difficult, but the dof even closer as well, may have made this even better, but would likely have diminished the illusion of the framing at the bottom.  Not sure, but perhaps a more finely tuned crop at the top, making a more horizontal framing.  More at the bottom (even if oof), possibly as well.  Selective desat may have given this extra as well, who knows - nice scene/candid as is, in my opinion.  +m in your title.', '2006-06-19 19:51:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529731, 347547, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - Nice scene/shot - not framed strongly enough for this Challenge in my opinion.  Maybe a tighter crop, who knows.</td>', '2 - Nice scene/shot - not framed strongly enough for this Challenge in my opinion.  Maybe a tighter crop, who knows.', '2006-06-19 19:53:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2529738, 347446, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - Possibly good potential, even using the oof fore framing.  Bigger (640 width) and a more balanced compostion/crop likely helped.</td>', '2 - Possibly good potential, even using the oof fore framing.  Bigger (640 width) and a more balanced compostion/crop likely helped.', '2006-06-19 19:54:55.000000', NULL, 1),
