(2535169, 344827, 23430, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by amit_saha:</b></div><hr/><i> Post contest...<br/> <br/>I misread the basic editing rules of using a single photo only. This picture would not have been feasible without either a ND Grad or multiple exposures/HDR in PS. I want to thank all of you who voted for this picture.<br/> <br/>I will be careful of this rule in my next entry.<br/>Thanks<br/>Amit<br/> <br/>PS: If I read the basic editing rule correctly, even if I had used the ND Grad, it would have been DQ''d? Is this understanding correct? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>A filter placed on the camera is fine but the equivalent effect carried out in editing is not.<br/> <br/>Nice pic by the way.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-21 04:46:33.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by amit_saha: Post contest... I misread the basic editing rules of using a single photo only. This picture would not have been feasible without either a ND Grad or multiple exposures/HDR in PS. I want to thank all of you who voted for this picture. I will be careful of this rule in my next entry.ThanksAmit PS: If I read the basic editing rule correctly, even if I had used the ND Grad, it would have been DQ''d? Is this understanding correct?  A filter placed on the camera is fine but the equivalent effect carried out in editing is not. Nice pic by the way.', '2006-06-21 05:45:27.000000', '2006-06-21 05:46:33.000000', 0),
